{
    "name": "Battery Level Indicator (Green/Yellow/Red)",
    "description": "A battery fuel gauge: as the battery sags 4.2V→3.0V, a zener reference + ladder and window comparators light EXACTLY ONE of three LEDs — green above 3.7V, yellow 3.4–3.7V, red below 3.4V. The measured handoffs land within 10mV of the 3.70/3.40 design points (the small offsets are real comparator input-loading physics). Run the transient and watch the green→yellow→red handover. (ngspice-validated: one LED at a time, correct thresholds.)",
    "tags": ["sensor", "battery", "monitor", "led", "window-comparator", "zener"],
    "analysisConfig": {
        "analysis": {
            "type": "tran",
            "stopTime": "12",
            "stepTime": "5m"
        },
        "probes": ["i(R7)", "i(R8)", "i(R9)", "v(vbat)", "v(vdiv)", "v(refh)", "v(refl)"]
    },
